# 4. MCP INTENT COMPILER (P-006 EXTENSION)

## 4.1 Input Format

```json
{
  "intent": "string",
  "source": "jarvis | ayre | gpt | codex",
  "type": "memory | event | decision | patch | sync | query",
  "scope": "supabase | github | hybrid | local",
  "payload": {}
}
```

---

## 4.2 Compilation Rules

### Rule 1 — Tool Minimization

* max 1 Supabase call per logical action
* max 1 GitHub call per commit cycle
* batch memory writes

---

### Rule 2 — Routing Collapse

If multiple systems requested:

```
Supabase + GitHub + Memory
→ must collapse into single SKADI transaction batch
```

---

### Rule 3 — God System Fusion

Instead of sequential calls:

```
ODIN → KRONOS → AEGIS → SKADI
```

MCP compiles into:

```
one execution plan with embedded metadata
```

---

# 5. CONNECTOR UNIFICATION (SUPABASE + GITHUB)

## 5.1 Single Write Contract

ALL writes must go through:

```
MCP → SKADI → CONNECTOR ROUTER
```

Router branches internally:

| Target    | Handler                  |
| --------- | ------------------------ |
| Supabase  | event/memory/ledger sink |
| GitHub    | commit/push patch        |
| MCP tools | query interface only     |

---

## 5.2 No Direct Writes Rule

Forbidden:

* direct Supabase calls outside SKADI
* direct GitHub API calls outside MCP
* bypassing ODIN classification

Allowed:

* MCP compiled execution plan only

---

